{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"DestinationTesting"}],"title":"DestinationTesting","role":"collection","externalID":"DestinationTesting","symbolKind":"module"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Check from Swift Testing that a vendor destination keeps the library’s rules and sends what its fixtures record.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance","type":"reference"},{"text":" runs the checks every vendor destination must pass, through a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ScriptedTransport","type":"reference"},{"text":" that keeps each request and answers from a script rather than the network:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"its requests match recorded fixtures byte for byte;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is sent only after the adopter opts in, and only while the record reveals it;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"behind a tracker’s consent and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accepting(_:)"},{"text":", it sends exactly the records it is handed;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"a record over the vendor’s limit is left out and reported, and the rest of its batch is sent;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no response, a 5xx, 408, 429 and each status of the encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"transientStatuses","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are retried,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and other failures are dropped and reported;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a 2xx answer whose body the encoder can’t read, an empty one included, counts as delivered: sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once, nothing reported;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"no request carries a trace context in its header fields, even while a tracer is active.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make it with the vendor’s limit and a closure that calls the vendor’s factory with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationSetup","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"‘s plan, transport and backoff. Every check’s records are tracked at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"setup’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"},{"type":"text","text":"; a factory whose encoder leaves out records by their age takes it as the time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it encodes at, so the checks pass whenever the test runs. Run each "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as a test"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"case of its own:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import DestinationTesting","import Foundation","import HTTPDestinations","import PostHogEncoding","import Testing","","@Test(arguments: ConformanceCheck.allCases)","func postHogConformance(check: ConformanceCheck) async throws {","    let host = try #require(URL(string: \"https:\/\/posthog.example.com\"))","    let conformance = DestinationConformance(limit: PostHogBatchEncoder.batchLimit) { setup in","        try HTTPDestination.postHog(projectToken: \"phc_test\", host: host, plan: setup.plan, transport: setup.transport, backoff: setup.backoff)","    }","    try await conformance.expect(check)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each check records a Swift Testing issue for every rule the destination breaks. A project’s own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tests write their assertions out in full. This one is shared on purpose, as TrackingPlanTesting’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectTrackingPlan(_:matches:sourceLocation:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is, so every vendor module runs the same checks."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It imports Swift Testing, so add it to test targets only. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves it out."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/writingavendordestination","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers the module these checks test.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance","doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck","doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationSetup"],"anchor":"Checking-a-destination","title":"Checking a destination"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ScriptedTransport"],"anchor":"Sending-without-a-network","title":"Sending without a network"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/destinationtesting"]}],"references":{"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting":{"title":"DestinationTesting","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting","url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Check from Swift Testing that a vendor destination keeps the library’s rules and sends what its fixtures record."}],"role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/ConformanceCheck":{"title":"ConformanceCheck","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConformanceCheck"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"One rule every vendor destination keeps, which ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance\/expect(_:sourceLocation:)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"checks.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/conformancecheck","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConformanceCheck"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/DestinationSetup":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DestinationSetup","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DestinationSetup","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/destinationsetup","abstract":[{"text":"What a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance"},{"text":" check hands the vendor’s factory: the plan of the events it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sends, the transport to send them through, a backoff short enough that a retry doesn’t hold the","type":"text"},{"